still mad about how Game of Thrones went  down fear not House of the Dragon has  got your back keep watching to find out  why you should give it a shot Game of  Thrones took a heavy hit following the  release of its eighth season the show's  final episodes were penned by fans many  of whom criticized the story's rushed  pacing and many attempts to subvert  audiences expectations so what went  wrong well for one thing the white  walkers were defeated in one episode  after eight seasons of build up and if  you thought the night King stared down  with Jon Snow in season 5's hard home  guaranteed an epic final fight between  the two well think again Arya Stark is  the one to take out the night King in  the show while Jon is preoccupied with  the undead dragon viserion but that's  not all the Revelation that Jon is  actually aegon Targaryen trueborn son of  rhaegar Targaryen and lyanna Stark  ultimately leads to nothing Jon never  ascends the Iron Throne or fulfills the  prophecy of the prince that was promised  meanwhile Daenerys Targaryen flips from  Misa to Mad Queen in one harrowing  episode which sees her Slaughter the  civilians of King's Landing with  Dragonfire oh and Jaime Lannister  abandons Brienne of Tarth to die with  his sister and lover Cersei in the end  Bran Stark emerges From the Ashes as the  new king of Westeros because reasons and  who has a better story  than bran the broken naturally all of  this led many Game of Thrones fans to  vow that they were finished with the  once esteemed fantasy franchise  so far only one aspect of the Game of  Thrones finale has been confirmed to  come from Martin himself King bran  during a 2019 interview published by HBO  actor Isaac Hempstead writes stated  David benioff and Dan Weiss told me  there were two things George R.R Martin  had planned for bran and that was the  Hodor Revelation and that he would be  king so that's pretty special to be  directly involved in something that is  part of George's Vision unless Martin  changes his mind fans can't expect to  see bran on the throne in the books as  well as in the show everything else  however that remains questionable Martin  has even said that fans know unending  but not the ending it's certainly easy  for fans to remain hopeful for a more  satisfying conclusion to the novels  fortunately House of the Dragon seems to  be rebuilding Bridges with its spurned  audience a prequel to Game of Thrones  House of the Dragon takes place 172  years before Daenerys targaryen's birth  and documents one of the most turbulent  times in her family's history the period  of civil war known as the dance of the  dragons for fans who loved the political  drama and Scandals of Game of Thrones  this is the perfect successor show to  scratch that itch during its Premiere  episode House of the Dragon places as  much emphasis on the Song of Ice and  Fire as it does Game of Thrones in Heirs  of the Dragon King viserys informs his  daughter rhaenyra about a prophetic  dream of their ancestor aegons that  spurred him to conquer Westeros with his  Dragon Valerian the black dread aegon  called his dream The Song of Ice and  Fire King viserys passes on aegon's  vision of a terrible winter gusting out  of the distant North which prompted the  Conqueror to create the iron throne and  unify the kingdoms under Targaryen rule  it's an interesting tidbit that further  fleshes out the story of the others but  why did the showrunners Ryan condle and  Miguel sapochnik choose to include a  prophecy about the white walkers in a  show about House Targaryen particularly  in its first episode  as it turns out aegon the conqueror's  prophecy comes from none other than  George R.R Martin the author confirmed  his involvement with House of the Dragon  early on while showrunner Ryan Condell  spoke to Esquire about collaborating  with Martin he said George hired me and  I came to this as a fan he was very  involved with the beginning of the show  obviously it does not exist without him  he wrote the original Source material  condole continued this was the successor  show that I think he was most interested  in of all the ones that HBO was  considering and exploring certainly in  the very beginning in the conceptual  phase George was very involved in an  interview with the New York Times Martin  compared his involvement with House of  the Dragon to Game of Thrones remarking  how he was kept out of the loop during  the later seasons of Thrones he claimed  by season 5 and 6 and certainly seven  and eight I was pretty much out of the  loop I don't know why you have to ask  showrunners Dan and Dave with Martin at  the helm House of the Dragon offers the  chance to tell a story more faithful to  the author's original vision  thanks to George R Martin's involvement  House of the Dragon seems to be Bridging  the Gap between show and book Canon for  example aegon's prophecy makes no  mention of anything to symbolize Arya  Stark as the savior of humanity end the  last Scions of House Targaryen don't  really phase the night King in Game of  Thrones as Daenerys and drogon quickly  discover the icy villain is fireproof  while Jon is overwhelmed by Undead  soldiers before he can take a swing at  any white walkers it's certainly  possible that aegon's prophecy in House  of the Dragon isn't supposed to  foreshadow The Game of Thrones finale in  2019 before season 8 aired Martin  revealed to Entertainment Weekly that he  hadn't read any scripts for The Final  Season stating there's a lot of minor  character arcs they'll be coming up with  on their own and of course they passed  me several years ago there may be  important discrepancies more recently  Martin confirmed on his blog that his  ending will be different adding not all  of the characters who survived until the  end of game of drones will survive until  the end of A Song of Ice and Fire and  not all of the characters who died on  Game of Thrones will die in A Song of  Ice and Fire before House of the Dragon  HBO almost greenlit another prequel to  follow season 8 of Game of Thrones the  planned series titled blood moon was to  take place 8 000 years before the events  of the original show Jurgen era known as  The Age of Heroes what was blood moon  about in summary the white walkers this  prequel would have depicted the first  long night eight centuries before the  night King's defeat at Winterfell with  the white walkers descending on Humanity  from the far north for the very first  time according to HBO blood moon was  going to be seriously epic in scope the  first press release stated from the  horrifying secrets of westeros's History  to the true origin of the white walkers  the mysteries of the East to the Starks  of Legend it's not the story we think we  know Jane Goldman was to serve as  showrunner alongside George RR Martin as  an executive producer while Naomi Watts  had been cast in the lead role sadly  blood moon never made it past production  a pilot episode was filmed but the  series was shelved in favor of House of  the Dragon given that blood moon was  supposed to focus on the long night and  the origin of the white walkers it's  possible that aegon's prophecy or  whatever inspired it would have been  heavily involved in that series  it's worth noting that HBO doesn't  necessarily need blood moon to redeem  the series finale along with a slate of  prequel shows George R Martin confirmed  on his blog that a sequel to Game of  Thrones is currently in the pipeworks  not much is known so far but the sequel  but what fans do know is that the  planned series is Jon Snow Centric with  actor kit Harrington leading the project  You Know Nothing Jon Snow official news  of the Jon Snow sequel first broke in a  piece for The Hollywood Reporter Emilia  Clark later verified in an interview  with the BBC that Harrington essentially  created the show and that he is in it  from the ground up there are no  guarantees that the Jon Snow sequel will  make it out of pre-production still if  the series does make it to the small  screen it could retcon parts of season  8. it might even correspond with aegon's  prophecy in House of the Dragon a sequel  starring Jon Snow AKA aegon Targaryen  could very well feature the return of  the white walkers led by a new icy  villain for him to face  Game of Thrones could also be brought  back to the small screen in animation  according to George R Martin's blog an  animated prequel set in the distant land  of essos is also in the early stages of  pre-production the Golden Empire of vidi  inspired by Imperial China predates both  old valyria and the long night some fans  speculate that it was the gemstone  Emperors of Yeti who taught the  valyrians how to control dragons Corliss  valarian made the long perilous Voyage  to yidi in his youth something that  viewers could witness if his prequel  series is greenlit if HBO branches into  animation with its Yeti series then it's  also possible fans could see an animated  adaptation of A Song of Ice and Fire in  the future animation requires a less  Hefty budget too something that might  appeal to HBO after it spent 90 million  dollars on the final season of Game of  Thrones this is one way that Thrones  could return bigger and bloodier than  ever  the inclusion of aegon's Prophecy 2  House of the Dragon doesn't appear to be  a fluke a weeks ahead trailer released  on the official Game of Thrones YouTube  channel has teased even more prophecies  in the show in the teaser Millie  alcock's raniera Targaryen appears to be  reading more of aegon the conqueror's  documented prophetic dreams as she  States from my blood  [Music]  come the prince that was promised this  is big news for readers of the books in  the second novel a Clash of Kings  Daenerys Ventures into the house of the  undying to seek counsel from the  mysterious warlocks of karth Daenerys  consumes a psychedelic substance known  as shade of the evening and experiences  multiple prophetic Visions in one a  brutalized woman represents war-torn  Westeros another features the wolf King  at a feast foreshadowing the Red Wedding  several others include Snippets from the  past and the future of Martin's world  one such moment includes her brother  rhaegar talking with an unknown woman  about their newborn son during the scene  rhaegar speaks the same words that  rhaenyra speaks in the house of the  Dragon trailer it seems that house of  the Dragon will be tackling this crucial  plot thread sometime in the future  despite the fact that it apparently has  little to do with the main events of the  show with the runway success of House of  the Dragon the future of the Game of  Thrones franchise suddenly looks more  optimistic George R Martin's enthusiasm  for the prequel is gradually encouraging  fans trust again after the disastrous  final season of Game of Thrones and the  extra efforts taken to adhere to  Buchanan aren't exactly hurting either  HBO seems to be focusing on filling out  the world too with various prequels and  spin-offs set in Westeros and essos  lined up if any of them matched the  early success of House of the Dragon  then it's likely the streaming Titan  will go all in on building a potential  Martin Cinematic Universe if that  happens then revisiting the apocalyptic  threat from the far north sounds far too  good a spectacle to pass on whether it's  down to a Jon Snow sequel another  prequel or simply a plot thread followed  by a house of the Dragon there's a good  chance that the events of the final  season of Game of Thrones will one day  feel like nothing more than a bad dream  [Music]
 

